---
<ArticleLayout
  title="Whole House Generator Installation: What to Expect"
  description="Learn how whole house generator installation works, from load and site assessment through permits, fuel and electrical work, commissioning and homeowner handoff."
  category="Installation" categoryHref="/installation/" updated="2026-10-04" verified="2026-10-04" image="/images/install-crew-setting-unit.webp" readingTime="9 min read" toc={toc}
  takeaways={[
    'A site-specific load assessment, exact model/manual review, and written installation scope should come before purchase.',
    'Permits, utilities, clearances, and local approvals vary; do not assume one national schedule or checklist applies everywhere.',
    'Startup, transfer testing, documentation, and owner instruction belong in the handoff plan.',
  ]}
  sources={[
    { label: 'Generac: home standby installation process and cost overview', href: 'https://www.generac.com/resources/home-management/backup-generator-installation/', type: 'Manufacturer', verified: '2026-10-04' },
