        <desc id="install-flow-desc">Assessment and equipment selection lead to written scope and approvals, then professional site work and connections, then inspection, commissioning, and owner handoff.</desc>
        <defs><marker id="arrow-install" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="8" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L0,6 L9,3 z" fill="#1b3a6b" /></marker></defs>
        <g font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" text-anchor="middle">
          <rect x="10" y="42" width="174" height="116" rx="14" fill="#edf3fb" stroke="#1b3a6b" stroke-width="2"/><text x="97" y="82" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="#1b3a6b">Assess</text><text x="97" y="108" font-size="13" fill="#27364d">loads, fuel, panel,</text><text x="97" y="128" font-size="13" fill="#27364d">site and model</text>
          <rect x="210" y="42" width="174" height="116" rx="14" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2"/><text x="297" y="82" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="#8a4300">Document</text><text x="297" y="108" font-size="13" fill="#27364d">written scope, permits,</text><text x="297" y="128" font-size="13" fill="#27364d">utility / property approvals</text>
          <rect x="410" y="42" width="174" height="116" rx="14" fill="#fff7ed" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="2"/><text x="497" y="82" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="#8a4300">Install</text><text x="497" y="108" font-size="13" fill="#27364d">qualified electrical,</text><text x="497" y="128" font-size="13" fill="#27364d">fuel and site work</text>
          <rect x="610" y="42" width="174" height="116" rx="14" fill="#e9f5ee" stroke="#237a4b" stroke-width="2"/><text x="697" y="82" font-size="16" font-weight="700" fill="#14532d">Verify & hand off</text><text x="697" y="108" font-size="13" fill="#27364d">inspection, test, records</text><text x="697" y="128" font-size="13" fill="#27364d">and owner instructions</text>
          <line x1="184" y1="100" x2="205" y2="100" stroke="#1b3a6b" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arrow-install)"/><line x1="384" y1="100" x2="405" y2="100" stroke="#1b3a6b" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arrow-install)"/><line x1="584" y1="100" x2="605" y2="100" stroke="#1b3a6b" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#arrow-install)"/>
          <text x="400" y="196" font-size="14" fill="#374151">Local sequence, work time, and approvals depend on the project.</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600">Original editorial diagram; it does not describe wiring or fuel-line installation instructions.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="commissioning">
    <h2>5. Inspection, commissioning, and handoff</h2>
    <p>Before the contractor leaves, confirm the required authority inspection has occurred or has a documented schedule. Ask the installer to explain the correct operating modes and demonstrate the system’s manufacturer-prescribed startup/transfer test.</p>
    <p>Request the final model/serial details, permits/inspection records, manuals, warranty and registration information, operating limits, maintenance schedule, service contact, and instructions for alarms or shutdowns. Keep the written load/transfer configuration and any approved changes with the records.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="timeline">
    <h2>Project timing depends on preparation and approvals</h2>
    <p>Generac says physical installation usually takes hours, while preparation may take multiple weeks; dealer availability, site preparation, gas work, and permits affect timing. That is a manufacturer’s general description—not a guaranteed schedule for another brand, contractor, or jurisdiction.</p>
    <p>Ask for a written schedule that distinguishes equipment availability, permit/utility approval, site preparation, on-site work, inspection, and commissioning. Storm-related demand or local backlogs may change the dates.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="checklist">
    <h2>Homeowner checklist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Keep access clear to the panel, fuel equipment, and planned generator site during scheduled work.</li>
      <li>Confirm pets/children remain clear of the work area and identify any temporary utility interruption in advance.</li>
      <li>Obtain written confirmation of each permit/inspection responsibility.</li>
      <li>Do not operate the generator until it has been installed, inspected as required, and commissioned according to the manufacturer instructions.</li>
      <li>Save the final documents and set reminders based on the exact manufacturer maintenance schedule.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</ArticleLayout>
